#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hollow Station: the siege of a mining colony on Calyx, 2290.  A sample
game for the Grognard engine, and an original one.

The miners of Hollow Station cut into a cavern under the ice of Calyx
and woke what lived there.  Now it is coming up out of the burrows, more
of it every hour, and the relief shuttle is nine hours out.  The
colony's security troopers, miners with cutting lasers and two sentry
turrets must hold the domes, seal what burrows they can, and get the
colonists onto the landing pad when the shuttle comes down.  Play
either side against the computer, or against a friend at the same
screen.

Run it with ./hollow (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.hollow.json.  ./hollow --selftest checks the map and plays
a game between two computer players.
"""

